# Website grounding rules

- Company doctrine lives in private `Axon-Enjin/company-docs`.
- For customer-facing copy and IA, read only `docs/grounding/` — especially `WEBSITE-CONTRACT.md`, `COMMERCIAL-MODEL-V2.md`, and `SITEMAP.md`.
- IA is two-property: `axonenjin.com` (company) and `axlefield.axonenjin.com` (product). Do not merge them into one public nav.
- Never invent prices, compliance claims, or payment acceptance.
- No peso/currency amounts on the public site (F-34).
- Ventures are secondary on the **company** site (Collaborate / footer only). Never on Axlefield primary nav or as an equal CTA.
- If grounding conflicts with live HTML, flag it — do not silently invent a third doctrine.
- Do not treat `docs/_retired-to-company-docs/` as source of truth.
